title: 'transaction-storage-proof: read only the selected transaction'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    The storage-proof prover now picks the chunk from the transaction sizes returned by
    `TransactionStorageApi::indexed_transactions` (v2) and loads only the transaction that holds it,
    instead of reading the target block's whole indexed body. Runtimes with API v1 keep the old path.
crates:
- name: sp-transaction-storage-proof
  bump: minor
- name: sc-service
  bump: patch
- name: polkadot-omni-node-lib
  bump: patch
